==English==
[[File:Opossum_2.jpg|thumb|An '''opossum'''.]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|pim|en}} {{term|aposoum||white animal|lang=pim}}, from {{etyl|alg-pro|en}} {{m|alg-pro|*wa·p-aʔɬemwa||white dog}}; compare Ojibwe {{term|waabasim|lang=oj||white dog|sc=Latn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/əˈpɒsəm/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|ə-päsʹəm}}, {{IPA|/əˈpɑsəm/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|o|pos|sum|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any [[American]] [[marsupial]] of the [[family]] [[Didelphidae]]. The common species of the United States is ''[[Didelphis virginiana]]''.

====Synonyms====
* [[possum]] {{qualifier|US}}

====Derived terms====
* [[water opossum]] ({{taxlink|Chironectes minimus|species|noshow=1}})<!-- of Brazil, which has the hind feet webbed, is provided with a marsupial pouch and with cheek pouches. It is called also [[yapock]].-->
* [[opossum mouse]]<!-- See [[flying mouse]]-->
* [[opossum rat]] ({{taxlink|Rattus marmosurus|species|noshow=1}})
* [[opossum shrimp]]<!-- any schizopod crustacean of the genus Mysis and allied genera. See [[schizopoda]].-->

